// endpoint_comment_on_pull_request.proto — CommentOnPullRequest: post a
// comment on a pull request for a workspace, so the workspace is never told
// its own words back. AGENT API section.
//
// WHY THE DAEMON POSTS. An agent posts under the user's own GitHub login, so
// by author alone the daemon cannot tell an agent's reply from the user's
// comment, and the user's comments must keep waking the agent: commenting on
// the agent's pull request is how the user talks to it in public. So the
// agent posts through the daemon, which records the created comment's id
// against the workspace's subscription in the same transaction that answers,
// and the poll never tells a subscriber an item recorded as its own. A reply
// an agent posts any other way is told back to it as an ordinary comment.

